"""The prose claims of REPORT.md and where each comes from.

Each entry: (text that must stand in REPORT.md, [sources]). A source is one of
  ("src", file, needle)            the needle must stand on a line of the committed file; the checker finds the line
  ("src", file, needle, anchor)    the same, on the first matching line at or after the first line holding the anchor
  ("cell", table, cell)            a cell of a generated table, already traced in build/trace_tables.tsv
  ("fact", key, expected)          a value in build/facts.json, computed by tools/build_tables.py
  ("git", rev-args, needle)        the needle must stand in `git <rev-args>` run read-only on the records worktree
  ("note", text)                   a statement about this report itself, or a reading that carries no number
No line number is typed here: check_trace.py finds each and writes it into TRACE.md.
"""
